<title>BELGIUM: BBL says ups stake in India's Vysya.</title>
<headline>BBL says ups stake in India's Vysya.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgium's Bank Brussels Lambert (BBL) said on Tuesday it had raised its equity interest in India's Vysya Bank to 10 from five percent.</p>
<p>BBL said Vysya was India's leading private bank, when measured either in terms of deposits, loans or profitability.</p>
<p>Vysya, based in Bangalore, has 343 branches and 100 other outlets, BBL said. Its own funds exceed five billion Belgian francs and its capital adequacy ratio is 14.2 percent.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
